# retroforge video codec links — /dev/video-enc0 for the hardware encoder, /dev/video-dec0 for the decoder.
#
# The SoCs' video block is a stateful V4L2 mem2mem device, driven by qcom-iris on every SoC we ship
# (SM6115 and SM4450 since 2026-11-23, kernel/patches/1095; venus before). Its nodes are
# /dev/videoN with N in probe order.
#
# The Steam UI's Chromium (libcef) decodes video through V4L2 only when /dev/video-dec0 exists when
# its GPU process starts. Every SoC gets the link (user, 2026-11-28), with the kernel patches that
# make Chromium's use of the decoder work:
#   - 1076-1078 (gen1 firmware: SM6115, SM8250) and 1079-1080 (gen2: SM8550, SM8650, SM8750): frames
#     the firmware decodes but does not show come back empty, and a loop or seek no longer stalls
#     the decoder. Without 1080 every video stopped after its first pass and Chromium then decoded
#     all of them in software; the 2026-10-29 Pocket FIT (SM8650) case, four cores at 95 C, was this
#     path before the fixes.
#   - 1097: every decoder reports the frame sizes it takes: AR50_LITE (SM6115, SM4450) 1920x1088, so
#     Steam's 1920x1200 startup movies stay in software there; SM8250 8192x4320; SM8550-SM8750
#     8192x4352, and 4096x2304 for VP9 (msm_vidc's limits).
#   - 1098: decoded frames are mapped cached where the video core is not cache-coherent (SM6115,
#     SM8250). Chromium reads every frame on the CPU: uncached, a 1080p30 VP9 clip on the MANGMI Air X
#     showed 180-188 of 300 frames at 167-175% CPU, worse than software; cached, 297-298 at 106-112%,
#     against software's 300 at 161-170%.
# KONKR Pocket FIT Elite (SM8750), 2026-11-28: 1080p VP9 in Steam's UI 299 of 300 frames at 45% of a
# core (software 56-60%), Steam's 1920x1200 startup movies 600 of 600 at 59-62% (software 75-76%).
# One run in about 40 left two of Chromium's threads spinning (cause not found). Retroid Pocket 5 (SM8250): the
# clips loop on the codec at the same CPU as software, as Chromium converts each decoded frame on the CPU.
# Steam's Remote Play client (streaming_client, CV4L2Accel) probes /dev/video0..99 as well as
# video-dec0..99, so it finds the decoder with or without a link.
# The names are iris's video_device names (iris_probe.c); the nodes keep systemd's root:video 0660,
# and the session user is in `video`.
SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", ATTR{name}=="qcom-iris-encoder", SYMLINK+="video-enc0"
SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", ATTR{name}=="qcom-iris-decoder", SYMLINK+="video-dec0"
